 "final_message": "All eleven items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20133 (`metrics.py`):**\n  - `monitor_flag_rate` counts only `True` as flagged. It returns `0.0` for an empty list.\n  - `pooled_flag_rate` now divides total flagged by total transcripts across all groups. It returns `0.0` when there are none.\n  - `flags_in_window` sums the last `days` entries, and `days == 0` gives `0`.\n- **Items 4\u20135 (`parse_transcript_log`):**\n  - `1`, `0` and empty now map to `True`, `False` and `None`.\n  - Blank, whitespace-only and `#` lines are skipped.\n  - Whitespace around fields is ignored.\n- **Item 6 (`dedupe_transcripts`):** the last record for an id wins.\n- **Item 7 (`daily_flag_counts`):** it returns one entry per day from `start_day` to `end_day`, with zeros for empty days. Out-of-range transcripts are ignored, and `end_day < start_day` gives an empty list.\n- **Item 8 (`monitor_summary`):** the rate is rounded to 3 places, and `groups` counts only non-empty groups.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added tests for `None` counting as not flagged and for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **Item 11 (README):** I fixed the `flags_in_window` entry and added `daily_flag_counts`. I also changed the `dedupe_transcripts` entry to say it keeps the last duplicate.\n\nSPEC section 4 only defines `1`, `0` and empty for `flagged`. I made any other value raise a `ValueError` instead of guessing; say if you'd rather it be handled differently.",
